es.sort(key=lambda box: box[0])\n","\n","# Print the number of potential bars found and their bounding boxes for inspection.\n","print(f\"Found {len(potential_bar_boxes)} potential histogram bars using Canny and filtering.\")\n","# print(\"Potential bar bounding boxes (x, y, w, h):\")\n","# for box in potential_bar_boxes:\n","#     print(box)\n","\n","# Store the identified potential bar boxes\n","identified_bar_boxes = potential_bar_boxes"],"execution_count":25,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Found 190 potential histogram bars using Canny and filtering.\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"5c3363b7"},"source":["**Reasoning**:\n","I have identified potential histogram bars using Canny edge detection and contour filtering. The next step in the subtask is to determine the height of each of these identified bars. I will iterate through the list of identified potential bar bounding boxes and extract the height (the fourth element of the bounding box tuple).\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"956036bd","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1755608011128,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":9,"user":{"displayName":"Confoederatio","userId":"16561974736841499613"}},"outputId":"5f5439ca-82d7-4a03-8238-7dc7e7290463"},"source":["# Determine the height of each identified potential histogram bar\n","# The list of potential bar bounding boxes is stored in `identified_bar_boxes`.\n","potential_bar_heights = [box[3] for box in identified_bar_boxes]\n","\n","# Print the extracted heights for inspection.\n","print(\"Extracted potential histogram bar heights (in pixels):\")\n","print(potential_bar_heights)\n","\n","# Store the extracted bar heights for subsequent steps.\n","extracted_bar_heights = potential_bar_heights"],"execution_count":26,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Extracted potential histogram bar heights (in pixels):\n","[17, 44, 27, 23, 19, 39, 14, 36, 40, 36, 33, 38, 33, 38, 23, 22, 21, 20, 23, 22, 22, 22, 23, 22, 23, 22, 22, 23, 22, 22, 23, 22, 23, 22, 22, 23, 20, 19, 23, 23, 22, 27, 22, 22, 23, 23, 22, 23, 22, 22, 22, 22, 23, 23, 22, 20, 23, 22, 21, 22, 23, 22, 25, 20, 1667, 33, 36, 22, 30, 17, 15, 22, 22, 27, 35, 22, 15, 30, 31, 23, 31, 11, 22, 23, 27, 27, 33, 22, 30, 14, 22, 30, 17, 17, 30, 22, 30, 23, 14, 14, 22, 29, 17, 24, 22, 31, 22, 26, 22, 22, 25, 30, 33, 33, 54, 65, 65, 65, 30, 30, 27, 17, 34, 17, 22, 22, 15, 33, 65, 65, 81, 30, 23, 16, 21, 30, 14, 17, 25, 65, 17, 22, 36, 34, 30, 30, 22, 33, 30, 25, 22, 51, 23, 30, 31, 23, 14, 14, 22, 41, 81, 30, 36, 15, 14, 15, 30, 17, 22, 17, 22, 25, 22, 27, 49, 65, 75, 86, 14, 14, 12, 25, 35, 31, 22, 31, 20, 30, 22, 22]\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"35ec9cf3"},"source":["## Associate bar heights with site clusters\n","\n","### Subtask:\n","Associate the extracted potential bar heights with their corresponding site cluster labels based on their horizontal position in the image.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"5ab2dec4"},"source":["**Reasoning**:\n","Re-run OCR using `image_to_data` on the full processed image to get bounding box info for text, filter for potential site labels based on pattern and vertical position, sort the labels by x-coordinate, and then associate the extracted potential bar heights with their corresponding site cluster labels based on horizontal proximity.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"e2c1e496","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1755608038645,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":2047,"user":{"displayName":"Confoederatio","userId":"16561974736841499613"}},"outputId":"5afb5f05-6d2a-4e4f-cf2e-4b17771e0e18"},"source":["# Use OCR using `image_to_data` on the full processed image to get bounding box info for text.\n","# Use a configuration suitable for complex layouts (e.g., psm 3).\n","custom_config_full_data = r'--oem 3 --psm 3'\n","ocr_full_data = pytesseract.image_to_data(processed_image, output_type=pytesseract.Output.DICT, config=custom_config_full_data)\n","\n","# Extract text, confidence, and bounding box for each detected item\n","extracted_full_data = []\n","n_boxes_full = len(ocr_full_data['level'])\n","for i in range(n_boxes_full):\n","    text = ocr_full_data['text'][i].strip()\n","    conf = int(ocr_full_data['conf'][i])\n","    # Filter out empty strings or low confidence results (adjust threshold as needed)\n","    if text and conf > 60: # Increased confidence threshold\n","        x = ocr_full_data['left'][i]\n","        y = ocr_full_data['top'][i]\n","        w = ocr_full_data['width'][i]\n","        h = ocr_full_data['height'][i]\n","        extracted_full_data.append({'text': text, 'box': (x, y, w, h), 'confidence': conf})\n","\n","# Filter the extracted data to find potential site labels based on pattern and vertical position\n","potential_site_labels_full_ocr = []\n","# Estimate the vertical range where labels are expected (near the bottom)\n","# Use the shape of the original OpenCV image (`original_opencv_image`) for height.\n","image_height_full = original_opencv_image.shape[0]\n","label_expected_y_min = int(image_height_full * 0.75) # Assuming labels are in the bottom 25%\n","\n","# Define a regex pattern to find site names (Q- or G- followed by letters)\n","site_name_pattern_full_ocr = re.compile(r'([QG]-[A-Za-z]+)')\n","\n","for item in extracted_full_data:\n","    # Check if the text matches the site name pattern\n","    if site_name_pattern_full_ocr.match(item['text']):\n","        # Check if the item's vertical position is within the expected range for labels\n","        item_y = item['box'][1]\n","        if item_y > label_expected_y_min:\n","            potential_site_labels_full_ocr.append(item)\n","\n","# Sort potential site labels by their x-coordinate\n","potential_site_labels_full_ocr.sort(key=lambda item: item['box'][0])\n","\n","print(\"\\n--- Potential Site Labels and their bounding boxes (from full OCR data) ---\")\n","for label_info in potential_site_labels_full_ocr:\n","    print(f\"Text: {label_info['text']}, Box: {label_info['box']}, Confidence: {label_info['confidence']}\")\n","\n","\n","# --- Associate Bar Heights with Site Labels based on horizontal proximity ---\n","# Use the potential bar boxes from the previous steps (`identified_bar_boxes`).\n","# Use the extracted bar heights from the previous steps (`extracted_bar_heights`).\n","# Use the potential site labels with bounding boxes from the full OCR data.\n","\n","site_cluster_hectares_associated = {} # {site_name: [list of bar heights]}\n","\n","# Create a list of potential bar boxes with their original heights\n","potential_bars_with_heights = [(identified_bar_boxes[i], extracted_bar_heights[i])\n","                               for i in range(len(identified_bar_boxes))]\n","\n","# Sort potential bars by their x-coordinate (already done, but good to be explicit)\n","potential_bars_with_heights.sort(key=lambda item: item[0][0])\n","\n","print(\"\\n--- Associating Bars with Site Labels ---\")\n","\n","# Simple spatial association: find bars whose horizontal center is closest to the label's center\n","# within a certain vertical range (i.e., above the label).\n","# Adjust thresholds based on the scale of the image and potential OCR inaccuracies.\n","\n","label_bar_association_threshold_x_revised = 80 # Increased max horizontal distance between centers\n","label_bar_vertical_offset_max_revised = int(image_height_full * 0.5) # Bars should be significantly above labels\n","\n","associated_data_revised = {} # {site_name: [list of bar heights]}\n","\n","# Iterate through the potential site labels found from the full OCR data\n","for label_info in potential_site_labels_full_ocr:\n","    label_box = label_info['box']\n","    label_text = label_info['text']\n","    label_center_x = label_box[0] + label_box[2] // 2\n","    label_y = label_box[1]\n","\n","    # Find potential bars associated with this label\n","    associated_bars_heights_revised = []\n","    for bar_box, bar_height in potential_bars_with_heights:\n","        bar_x, bar_y, bar_w, bar_h = bar_box\n","        bar_center_x = bar_x + bar_w // 2\n","\n","        # Check if the bar is above the label and their horizontal centers are close\n","        # Also ensure the bar is not too close vertically, implying it's not part of the label text itself.\n","        if bar_y < label_y and (label_y - bar_y) < label_bar_vertical_offset_max_revised and abs(bar_center_x - label_center_x) < label_bar_association_threshold_x_revised:\n","             associated_bars_heights_revised.append(bar_height)\n","\n","    if associated_bars_heights_revised:\n","        # Store the associated heights under the site label text\n","        associated_data_revised[label_text] = associated_bars_heights_revised\n","        print(f\"Associated {len(associated_bars_heights_revised)} bars with label '{label_text}'. Heights: {associated_bars_heights_revised}\")\n","\n","\n","print(\"\\n--- Associated Site Cluster Data (Heuristic) ---\")\n","print(associated_data_revised)\n","\n","# Acknowledge the limitations again\n","print(\"\\n--- Limitations ---\")\n","print(\"The association of bar heights with site cluster labels is based on spatial proximity heuristics and OCR accuracy.\")\n","print(\"Manual verification of the 'associated_data_revised' dictionary is strongly recommended.\")\n","\n","# Store the associated data for the next step\n","associated_site_hectares_raw = associated_data_revised"],"execution_count":27,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["\n","--- Potential Site Labels and their bounding boxes (from full OCR data) ---\n","Text: Q-Hualong, Box: (188, 1680, 201, 49), Confidence: 91\n","Text: Q-Xunhua, Box: (375, 1733, 173, 30), Confidence: 79\n","Text: Q-Ledu, Box: (551, 1680, 125, 49), Confidence: 92\n","Text: Q-Minhe, Box: (804, 1729, 146, 46), Confidence: 90\n","Text: G-Lanzhou, Box: (1091, 1681, 209, 49), Confidence: 91\n","Text: G-Linxia, Box: (1311, 1729, 154, 46), Confidence: 92\n","Text: G-Dingxi, Box: (1546, 1680, 154, 49), Confidence: 82\n","Text: G-Gannan, Box: (1808, 1729, 188, 46), Confidence: 92\n","Text: G-Longnan, Box: (2088, 1685, 190, 38), Confidence: 92\n","Text: G-Tianshui, Box: (2360, 1733, 184, 30), Confidence: 91\n","\n","--- Associating Bars with Site Labels ---\n","Associated 3 bars with label 'Q-Hualong'. Heights: [17, 22, 27]\n","Associated 4 bars with label 'Q-Xunhua'. Heights: [11, 22, 27, 27]\n","Associated 3 bars with label 'Q-Ledu'. Heights: [14, 17, 17]\n","Associated 7 bars with label 'Q-Minhe'. Heights: [14, 14, 17, 22, 22, 22, 22]\n","Associated 2 bars with label 'G-Lanzhou'. Heights: [17, 22]\n","Associated 3 bars with label 'G-Linxia'. Heights: [81, 14, 17]\n","Associated 2 bars with label 'G-Gannan'. Heights: [51, 14]\n","Associated 5 bars with label 'G-Longnan'. Heights: [14, 17, 17, 25, 22]\n","Associated 4 bars with label 'G-Tianshui'. Heights: [86, 14, 14, 35]\n","\n","--- Associated Site Cluster Data (Heuristic) ---\n","{'Q-Hualong': [17, 22, 27], 'Q-Xunhua': [11, 22, 27, 27], 'Q-Ledu': [14, 17, 17], 'Q-Minhe': [14, 14, 17, 22, 22, 22, 22], 'G-Lanzhou': [17, 22], 'G-Linxia': [81, 14, 17], 'G-Gannan': [51, 14], 'G-Longnan': [14, 17, 17, 25, 22], 'G-Tianshui': [86, 14, 14, 35]}\n","\n","--- Limitations ---\n","The association of bar heights with site cluster labels is based on spatial proximity heuristics and OCR accuracy.\n","Manual verification of the 'associated_data_revised' dictionary is strongly recommended.\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"a9519107"},"source":["## Calibrate pixel height to hectare value\n","\n","### Subtask:\n","Determine the relationship between pixel height and hectare value using the y-axis labels or scale present in the image.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"4b95820a"},"source":["**Reasoning**:\n","Crop the image to isolate the y-axis, perform OCR to extract numerical values and their positions, filter and sort these values, and then use them to determine the pixel-to-hectare calibration factor.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"2edb2cb1","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1755608065730,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":831,"user":{"displayName":"Confoederatio","userId":"16561974736841499613"}},"outputId":"335227d7-e963-40b2-d6c7-2970f6d0dc74"},"source":["# Crop the image to the left side where the y-axis and its labels are expected\n","# Estimate the region based on visual inspection of the image and previous OCR results.\n","# The y-axis labels seem to be on the left side, within the first 10-15% of the image width.\n","# Using the original_opencv_image for cropping.\n","image_width_full = original_opencv_image.shape[1]\n","crop_x_yaxis = int(image_width_full * 0.0) # Start from the left edge\n","crop_width_yaxis = int(image_width_full * 0.15) # Crop 15% of the width\n","cropped_image_yaxis = original_opencv_image[:, crop_x_yaxis : crop_x_yaxis + crop_width_yaxis]\n","\n","# Convert the cropped image to grayscale for OCR\n","gray_cropped_yaxis = cv2.cvtColor(cropped_image_yaxis, cv2.COLOR_BGR2GRAY)\n","\n","# Apply thresholding to the cropped y-axis image to improve OCR on numbers\n","# Use Otsu's thresholding as it often works well for separating text from background.\n","_, thresh_cropped_yaxis = cv2.threshold(gray_cropped_yaxis, 0, 255, cv2.THRESH_BINARY + cv2.THRESH_OTSU)\n","\n","# Use OCR (pytesseract) on the thresholded cropped image to extract text and data,\n","# including bounding boxes to get vertical positions.\n","# Use psm 6 for assuming a single uniform block of text, or psm 11 for sparse text.\n","# psm 6 seems to have worked reasonably well before.\n","custom_config_yaxis = r'--oem 3 --psm 6'\n","ocr_output_yaxis = pytesseract.image_to_data(thresh_cropped_yaxis, output_type=pytesseract.Output.DICT, config=custom_config_yaxis)\n","\n","# Extract text, confidence, and bounding box for each detected item\n","extracted_yaxis_data = []\n","n_boxes_yaxis = len(ocr_output_yaxis['level'])\n","for i in range(n_boxes_yaxis):\n","    text = ocr_output_yaxis['text'][i].strip()\n","    conf = int(ocr_output_yaxis['conf'][i])\n","    # Filter out empty strings or low confidence results\n","    if text and conf > 70: # Increased confidence threshold for numbers\n","        # Adjust x and y to be relative to the original image for consistency\n","        x = ocr_output_yaxis['left'][i] + crop_x_yaxis\n","        y = ocr_output_yaxis['top'][i]\n","        w = ocr_output_yaxis['width'][i]\n","        h = ocr_output_yaxis['height'][i]\n","        extracted_yaxis_data.append({'text': text, 'box': (x, y, w, h), 'confidence': conf})\n","\n","# Filter the extracted data to keep only numerical values that could be y-axis ticks.\n","# Numbers on the y-axis are expected to be integers and relatively large (e.g., 50, 100, 150).\n","yaxis_numerical_labels = []\n","for item in extracted_yaxis_data:\n","    # Try to convert the text to a number\n","    try:\n","        value = float(item['text']) # Use float to handle potential decimals if any, though integers are expected\n","        # Add a check to see if the number seems reasonable for a y-axis label in this context\n","        # Based on the image, values are in ranges like 0, 50, 100, 150. Let's assume values >= 0.\n","        if value >= 0: # Assuming hectare values are non-negative\n","             # Store the value and its vertical position (center of the bounding box, relative to original image)\n","            yaxis_numerical_labels.append({'value': value, 'y_pos': item['box'][1] + item['box'][3] // 2})\n","    except ValueError:\n","        # Not a valid number, ignore\n","        pass\n","\n","# Sort the numerical labels by their vertical position (y_pos), from top to bottom\n","yaxis_numerical_labels.sort(key=lambda item: item['y_pos'])\n","\n","print(\"\\n--- Extracted Y-axis Numerical Labels and Vertical Positions (Relative to Original Image) ---\")\n","for label_info in yaxis_numerical_labels:\n","    print(f\"Value: {label_info['value']}, Y-position (pixel): {label_info['y_pos']}\")\n","\n","# --- Determine the relationship between pixel height and hectare value ---\n","# This assumes a linear relationship, which is typical for a bar chart y-axis.\n","# We need at least two points (value, y_pos) to define the relationship.\n","# Ideally, we would use the origin (0, max_y_pixel) if detected.\n","# Let's use the top-most and bottom-most detected numerical labels assuming they represent\n","# a range on the y-axis. The bottom-most label is likely near the x-axis (0 hectares).\n","\n","pixel_to_hectare_calibration = None # Initialize to None\n","\n","if len(yaxis_numerical_labels) >= 2:\n","    # Use the lowest and highest detected y-axis values and their positions\n","    # The lowest y_pos corresponds to the highest hectare value on the chart (top of y-axis)\n","    # The highest y_pos corresponds to the lowest hectare value on the chart (bottom of y-axis, likely 0)\n","\n","    # Find the point closest to the bottom of the image (likely the origin or a low value)\n","    # The y-axis pixel coordinates increase downwards.\n","    # Using max y_pos for the bottom point, min y_pos for the top point.\n","    bottom_point = max(yaxis_numerical_labels, key=lambda item: item['y_pos'])\n","    top_point = min(yaxis_numerical_labels, key=lambda item: item['y_pos'])\n","\n","    print(f\"\\nUsing points for calibration: Bottom ({bottom_point['value']} ha, {bottom_point['y_pos']} px), Top ({top_point['value']} ha, {top_point['y_pos']} px)\")\n","\n","    # Calculate the pixel difference and hectare difference\n","    pixel_range = bottom_point['y_pos'] - top_point['y_pos']\n","    hectare_range = top_point['value'] - bottom_point['value'] # Hectare increases upwards\n","\n","    # Avoid division by zero if the detected points have the same y-position\n","    if pixel_range > 0:\n","        # Calculate the scale factor: hectares per pixel\n","        hectares_per_pixel = hectare_range / pixel_range\n","        print(f\"Calculated hectares per pixel: {hectares_per_pixel}\")\n","\n","        # We also need the hectare value at a reference pixel position.\n","        # Let's use the bottom point as the reference (likely 0 ha at its y_pos).\n","        pixel_to_hectare_calibration = {\n","            'hectares_per_pixel': hectares_per_pixel,\n","            'reference_y_pixel': bottom_point['y_pos'],\n","            'reference_hectare_value': bottom_point['value']\n","        }\n","        print(\"\\nPixel to Hectare Calibration Factor/Model:\")\n","        print(pixel_to_hectare_calibration)\n","\n","    else:\n","        print(\"\\nCould not determine a valid pixel-to-hectare relationship from the extracted y-axis labels (pixel range is zero).\")\n","\n","\n","else:\n","    print(\"\\nNot enough numerical labels detected on the y-axis to determine the pixel-to-hectare relationship.\")\n","\n","# Store the calibration factor for the next step\n","pixel_to_hectare_factor = pixel_to_hectare_calibration"],"execution_count":28,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["\n","--- Extracted Y-axis Numerical Labels and Vertical Positions (Relative to Original Image) ---\n","Value: 140.0, Y-position (pixel): 188\n","Value: 135.0, Y-position (pixel): 241\n","Value: 130.0, Y-position (pixel): 294\n","Value: 120.0, Y-position (pixel): 398\n","Value: 115.0, Y-position (pixel): 451\n","Value: 105.0, Y-position (pixel): 557\n","Value: 55.0, Y-position (pixel): 1083\n","Value: 50.0, Y-position (pixel): 1137\n","Value: 45.0, Y-position (pixel): 1190\n","Value: 40.0, Y-position (pixel): 1243\n","Value: 30.0, Y-position (pixel): 1348\n","Value: 25.0, Y-position (pixel): 1400\n","Value: 20.0, Y-position (pixel): 1453\n","Value: 45.0, Y-position (pixel): 1507\n","Value: 0.0, Y-position (pixel): 1664